{"name":"Grain of Salt","hex":"#d8dbe1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grain of salt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["With a little common sense and skepticism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grain_of_salt"}],"entries":[{"title":"A grain of salt","blocks":[{"text":"To take something with a \"grain of salt\" or \"pinch of salt\" is an English idiom that suggests to view something, specifically claims that may be misleading or unverified, with skepticism or not to interpret something literally."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/Naturalishistoria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_grain_of_salt","wikidata":"Q1143598"},{"title":"Grain","blocks":[{"text":"A grain is a small, hard, dry fruit (caryopsis)–with or without an attached hull layer–harvested for human or animal consumption. A grain crop is a grain-producing plant. The two main types of commercial grain crops are cereals and legumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Dhaniyangal.jpg/330px-Dhaniyangal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grain","wikidata":"Q2995529"},{"title":"Salt","blocks":[{"text":"Salt is a mineral composed primarily of sodium chloride (NaCl). When used in food, especially in granulated form, it is more formally called table salt. In the form of a natural crystalline mineral, salt is also known as rock salt or halite. Salt is essential for life in general, and saltiness is one of the basic human tastes. Salt is one of the oldest and most ubiquitous food seasonings, and is known to uniformly improve the taste perception of food. Salting, brining, and pickling are ancient and important methods of food preservation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Rock_salt_%28halitite%29_%28Billianwala_Salt_Member%2C_Salt_Range_Formation%2C_Ediacaran_to_Lower_Cambrian%3B_Khewra_Salt_Mine%2C_Salt_Range%2C_Pakistan%29_14.jpg/330px-Rock_salt_%28halitite%29_%28Billianwala_Salt_Member%2C_Salt_Range_Formation%2C_Ediacaran_to_Lower_Cambrian%3B_Khewra_Salt_Mine%2C_Salt_Range%2C_Pakistan%29_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt","wikidata":"Q11254"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Wheat-kernel_nutrition.png/120px-Wheat-kernel_nutrition.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Wheat-kernel_nutrition.png/250px-Wheat-kernel_nutrition.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Wheat-kernel_nutrition.png/120px-Wheat-kernel_nutrition.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWheat-kernel_nutrition.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Dinr%C3%AAyes.jpg/120px-Dinr%C3%AAyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Dinr%C3%AAyes.jpg/250px-Dinr%C3%AAyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Dinr%C3%AAyes.jpg/120px-Dinr%C3%AAyes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADinr%C3%AAyes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Gerstenkorrels_Hordeum_vulgare.jpg/120px-Gerstenkorrels_Hordeum_vulgare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Ger